# coverage.map — feature -> scenario(s) -> smoke map.
#
# Every feature the v2 model names (docs/V2_MODEL.md, tests/MANIFEST.md) has a
# row here. A row lists the full-suite scenarios that prove the feature and, via
# the scenario ids it names, the smoke list(s) that carry each one. Feature rows
# are checked by scripts/check-test-coverage.py:
#
#   * every scenario id named here must be an existing tests/agent/A*.sh or
#     tests/session/S*.sh (a row pointing at a missing scenario fails);
#   * every smoke-list entry must be named by at least one row, so the smoke can
#     never grow a scenario that maps to no feature;
#   * a row with no scenario in any smoke list must carry `full-only: <reason>`
#     (a feature with neither a full-suite-only note nor a smoke entry fails).
#
# Format: `feature | scenario ids | full-only: reason`
# The scenario ids are smoke ids (no `.sh`). `full-only:` is optional and is the
# only place a feature is allowed to have no smoke representation.
#
# Features whose scenarios are owned by a parallel lane (display-failures,
# gestures-gnome51, fractional-scaling, panel-sharing) have rows here built from
# the coverage that exists today; that lane extends the row when it lands and
# the guard keeps it honest.

